This master specification upgrades the initial DE RIDE v1.0 draft into an enterprise-grade, production-ready architecture engineered for a nationwide Nigerian rollout across all 36 states + FCT (with primary launch hub density in Ogun State and Lagos State), powered by a Go (Fiber) backend, Next.js 15 PWA frontend, Python (FastAPI + Groq) Amebo AI engine, Neon PostgreSQL + PostGIS, zero-cost in-app memory (no Redis until 5,000+ users), dual Biker ↔ Dispatch Rider mode switching, and an integrated Affordable Internet Data Subscription (VTU) module.
1. Brand Identity, Color System & UI/UX Architecture
Selected Color Palette: Logo-Matched Modern (High Contrast & Sleek)
Matched directly to your official DE RIDE brand mark (1794927085562.jpg), this palette delivers immediate visual continuity between the emblem and the UI while providing OLED battery savings for drivers/riders on long trips and razor-sharp contrast in bright outdoor motor parks.
 * Primary Background (Canvas): Deep Charcoal/Slate #1B2428
 * Elevated Surface / Cards / Bottom Sheets: Dark Gunmetal #243036 (1px border #324149)
 * Primary Navigation / Active Routes / Trust Accents: Ocean Teal #1A7D82 (Hover/Active: #229EA4)
 * Primary CTAs / Destination Pins / Alerts: Vibrant Coral #F46A6A (Hover/Active: #FF7E7E)
 * Primary Typography: Crisp Pure White #FFFFFF
 * Secondary Typography / Metadata: Cool Mist #9FB1B9
 * Success / Verified Badge / Online Status: Emerald Mint #10B981
 * Warning / Cooldown Timer / Grace Period: Solar Amber #F59E0B
UI/UX & App Layout Architecture (Low-Literacy & High-Speed Optimized)
 * App Shell & Navigation:
   * Persistent Top Header (56px): DE RIDE SVG Logo (left), Language & Voice Toggle (EN | YO | HA | IG | PCM with Web Speech API audio read-aloud icon), Amebo AI Token Pill (⚡ 10 Tokens), and—for dual-registered riders—a one-tap 🏍️ Biker ↔ 📦 Dispatch Mode Switcher.
   * Interactive Map Canvas (65% Viewport Height on Home): Custom dark-mode Google Maps (#1B2428 base geometry, #1A7D82 highway strokes, #F46A6A custom SVG park/destination pins).
   * Draggable Bottom Sheet (35%–85% Viewport Height): Snap-to-grid cards with minimum 48px × 48px touch targets, high-contrast progress bars for seat capacity (11/14 Seats), and visual iconography next to every label.
   * Bottom Navigation Bar (64px, 5 Tabs — Context-Aware by Portal):
     * Passenger: Explore Parks | My Tickets (QR) | Bike & Dispatch | Amebo AI | Data & Profile
     * Driver / Operator: Park Queue | QR Scanner | Trip Chat | Amebo AI | Earnings & Rank
     * Biker / Dispatch Rider: Live Radar | Active Job | Buy Data | Amebo AI | Wallet & Rank
2. Upgraded Core Business Logic & Operational Rules
2.1 Nationwide Rollout & Multi-Portal Architecture
 * Nationwide Scope (All 36 States + FCT): The database, PostGIS spatial queries, Google Maps geocoding, and state selectors support all 36 states + FCT from day one, with Ogun State and Lagos State pinned as primary launch hubs (e.g., Berger, Ojota, Oshodi, Jibowu, Maza-Maza, Abeokuta Kuto/Itoku, Sagamu Interchange, Ijebu-Ode, Sango-Ota).
 * Six Dedicated Portals + Dual Rider Switching:
   * Passenger Side (/(passenger)): Park discovery, bus seat booking, offline/online QR & manual ticket codes, refunds, passenger bike hailing, parcel dispatch ordering, trip chat, SOS escalation, Amebo AI, and affordable data bundles.
   * Bus Driver Side (/(driver)): Bus capacity/departure management (with 120s lock), opt-in GPS broadcasting, online/offline QR & manual code boarding scanner, trip chat, Amebo AI, and earnings.
   * Biker Side (/(biker)): Last-mile passenger bike hailing radar, navigation, chat, SOS, and instant switch to Dispatch Rider Mode.
   * Dispatch Rider Side (/(dispatch-rider)): Parcel/waybill pickup & delivery feed, receiver OTP/QR proof-of-delivery, navigation, and instant switch back to Biker Mode.
   * Park Operator & Terminal Dispatcher Side (/(park-operator)): Multi-bay terminal board, bus queue updates (120s lock), manual vs. GPS visibility toggle, driver/vehicle onboarding, and fleet settlements.
   * DE RIDE Admin Side (/(admin)): Nationwide live command map, immediate 3-way SOS escalation console, Cloudinary KYC approval queue, park/geofence management, and financial/VTU/Amebo audit logs.
 * Biker ↔ Dispatch Rider Dual-Registration & Switching:
   * A verified Biker can complete a streamlined 2-step Dispatch Rider Add-On KYC (uploading courier box photo & state dispatch permit to Cloudinary).
   * Once is_biker_verified = TRUE and is_dispatch_verified = TRUE, the rider can switch seamlessly between Biker Side and Dispatch Rider Side at any time (blocked only while an active ride or parcel delivery is in progress).
2.2 Park Visibility, Multi-Source GPS & 120-Second Cooldown Lock
 * Dual Visibility Mode:
   * Manual Park Queue Mode: Park Operators, Dispatchers, and Drivers manually log bus arrival, seat count, and scheduled departure.
   * Live GPS Telemetry Mode (Opt-In): Users explicitly opt in to background/foreground telemetry (explicitly acknowledging that the user pays for their own mobile data and battery usage). GPS coordinates stream via Go goroutine WebSockets from three prioritized sources:
     * Priority 1: Dedicated Vehicle OBD/GPS Hardware (HARDWARE).
     * Priority 2: Driver App (DRIVER_APP high-accuracy geolocation stream).
     * Priority 3: Dispatcher App (DISPATCHER_APP while bus is stationary inside park geofence).
 * 120-Second Capacity & Departure Lock (Zero-Cost In-App Memory Engine):
   * Whenever a Park Operator, Driver, or Dispatcher updates booked_seats or scheduled_departure_at, the Go backend sets an in-memory TTL lock (trip_lock:{trip_id}, 120 seconds) inside its thread-safe sync.RWMutex memory store and persists last_capacity_update_at in Neon PostgreSQL.
   * Any subsequent edit attempt within 120 seconds returns HTTP 429 (ERR_CAPACITY_COOLDOWN_ACTIVE) with retry_after_seconds, rendered as a live countdown ring in the UI.
2.3 Financial Engine, Fees & Refund/Cancellation Matrix
 * Checkout Breakdown (Passenger Pays All Fees Transparently):
   
   * Paystack Fee Formula (Nigeria): 1.5\% \text{ of subtotal} + ₦100 (₦100 waived for transactions under ₦2,500, local fee capped at ₦2,000), passed explicitly as paystack_fee.
 * Strict Refund & Cancellation Logic:
   * Non-Refundable Components: The ₦20 DE RIDE fee and the Paystack Processing Fee are NEVER refunded under any circumstance. All percentages below apply strictly to the Base Fare.
   * Refund Destination: User chooses at cancellation/claim time between Instant DE RIDE Wallet Credit (0 fee, immediate) or Original Funding Bank Account via Paystack Transfer API (settles within T+1).
| Scenario | Trigger Condition | Base Fare Refund % | DE RIDE ₦20 Fee | Paystack Fee |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Passenger Cancellation | Passenger cancels before bus departs / trip begins | 100% Refund | Non-Refundable | Non-Refundable |
| Late Arrival | Passenger arrives/scans > 10 minutes after scheduled/agreed departure time | 80% Refund | Non-Refundable | Non-Refundable |
| No-Show | Trip departs/completes with zero scan and zero prior cancellation | 40% Refund | Non-Refundable | Non-Refundable |
| Operator/Driver Cancellation | Bus trip cancelled by Park/Driver | 100% Refund (+ ₦20 credited) | Credited | Non-Refundable |
2.4 Real-Time Ephemeral Chat & Immediate Escalation Pipeline
 * Trip Chat Lifecycle: Automatically created when a trip opens for boarding (status = BOARDING). Accessible to paid ticket holders, the assigned Driver, and the Park Dispatcher.
 * 6-Minute Ephemeral Purge Rule: When a trip transitions to ARRIVED / COMPLETED, an in-process Go background ticker worker (chat_purge_worker.go) hard-deletes all rows in messages for that trip_id at arrived_at + 6 minutes—unless an active Dispute/Report flag is attached to the trip (which freezes the chat log into escalations.preserved_chat_log).
 * Immediate Real-Time Admin Escalation Path:
   * User taps Emergency / Report Issue inside Trip Chat or Active Ride screen.
   * WebSocket emits escalation:create immediately to the DE RIDE Live Admin Command Center with GPS coordinates, trip manifest, and recent messages.
   * Admin joins the live room within seconds (role: 'admin_mediator'), locking disputed funds in escrow and bridging communication directly between User \leftrightarrow DE RIDE Admin \leftrightarrow Issue / Driver / Dispatcher / Biker / Dispatch Rider in real time.
2.5 Affordable Internet Data Subscription Module (VTU Integration)
 * Because users pay for their own mobile data during GPS telemetry, live chat, and Amebo AI sessions, DE RIDE embeds an Affordable Internet Data Subscription storefront (/shared/buy-data) accessible to all roles (Passengers, Drivers, Bikers, Dispatch Riders, and Park Operators).
 * Architecture: Go backend fetches SME/Corporate Gifting/Direct data plans (MTN, AIRTEL, GLO, 9MOBILE) from your configurable VTU_BASE_URL and VTU_API_KEY, caches plan lists in In-App Memory (TTL: 15 minutes), and processes instant data vending via DE RIDE Wallet (with atomic PostgreSQL FOR UPDATE balance locking and automatic wallet rollback on vendor failure) or Paystack.
3. Tiered Subscription Ecosystem (Passengers, Drivers, Riders & Operators)
All users can start on a base tier and upgrade seamlessly at any time. Strict Rule Enforcement: The ₦60,000 One-Time Lifetime Plan is exclusively for Passengers (role === 'passenger'). Drivers, Dispatchers, Bikers, Dispatch Riders, and Park Operators are blocked at database, Go API (HTTP 403 ERR_ROLE_PLAN_RESTRICTED), and Next.js UI levels from purchasing the ₦60,000 one-time plan.
